#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:73 8f8a247c31c842e78475553124695ba1
msgid "2.1. Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:75 c954bd2ba2f84a8f8c68bc327fdae62a
msgid ""
"`findfmt` is compatible with all modern Linux distributions across "
"`x86_64`, `aarch64`, and `armv7l` architectures:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:78 9033356d26d043338f94c3acca3b79ae
msgid ""
"**Library Compatibility**: Works seamlessly on both `glibc`-based "
"distributions (Ubuntu, Debian, Fedora, openSUSE, Arch) and `musl`-based "
"distributions (Alpine Linux)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:81 807b2caa59174c92ae507df10850181e
msgid ""
"**User Binary PATH**: When installing via `uv tool install` or `pipx`, "
"ensure `~/.local/bin` is present in your shell `PATH`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:88 ad730c9a939c43959de08775ee5593c8
msgid ""
"**Paging Support**: Terminal paging automatically leverages your system "
"`PAGER` or `LESS` environment settings when output exceeds the terminal "
"window height."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:91 0159f06d543e4101a0169144a2d41cf8
msgid "2.2. macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:93 dccd7dad6ff04143b36f9715043dbca5
msgid ""
"`findfmt` supports macOS 12 (Monterey) and later across both Apple "
"Silicon (`arm64`) and Intel (`x86_64`) hardware:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:96 a58eae222358417a8e79ebfa6e26a266
msgid ""
"**Terminal Emulators**: Native macOS Terminal.app and third-party "
"emulators such as iTerm2 support ANSI color styling and clickable OSC 8 "
"terminal hyperlinks (`--hyperlink`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:99 3f7f7effa41a4e15921dd45a6c4f3c7e
msgid ""
"**File System Case-Sensitivity**: macOS defaults to APFS case-preserving "
"but case-insensitive semantics. Pattern searches (`-P`, `-I`) evaluate "
"patterns strictly unless `--ignore-case` is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:103 af24e247f9204bf58e52eee5c83ffd57
msgid ""
"**Homebrew Python**: Ensure that `uv` or `pipx` references your preferred"
" Python installation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:110 dba25a79b2c1418b906b9333d35fc2b0
msgid "2.3. Windows & Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:112 d69d913b94484c96b48484925f5ed275
msgid ""
"`findfmt` executes natively on Windows 10/11 and within Windows Subsystem"
" for Linux (WSL/WSL2):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:114 eaa8c00875c54be5a5f370d7e72b415b
msgid ""
"**Native Windows Execution**: Run `findfmt` within PowerShell, Command "
"Prompt, or Windows Terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:122 fc79536b5c7f4ffe9af5e197d67d62bc
msgid ""
"**Path Separators**: Both forward slashes (`/`) and backslashes (`\\`) "
"are recognized in path arguments. Output listings adhere to POSIX style "
"for cross-platform script consistency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:125 84c195750fa5461f983b8c5ac2e4426c
msgid ""
"**Symbolic Link Permissions**: Following directory symlinks (`-l` or "
"`--follow-links`) on native Windows requires either Windows Developer "
"Mode enabled or an elevated Administrator prompt due to underlying "
"Windows security policies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:129 9959f005ad7849faa35afe38707bb520
msgid ""
"**Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL2)**: For workflows tightly coupled "
"with Unix pipes and shell scripts, running `findfmt` inside WSL2 provides"
" native Linux filesystem performance and POSIX semantics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:133 140c72ceae1b4c0ab9315f2d594ba541
msgid "2.4. Docker & Container Environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:135 fb5d9704b98e486b9bb13f5f63ca36f8
msgid ""
"When executing `findfmt` within containerized pipelines, mount your "
"project directory into the container workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/installation.md:152 770242b0455545a6a59283b68ba59a52
msgid ""
"[!TIP] Mount project source directories with the read-only flag (`:ro` or"
" `:ro,Z` for container volume labels) to guarantee that discovery "
"operations cannot mutate repository files."
msgstr ""

